1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,300
Jim: Hello, South City Cycling Club.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:11,000
Woman: Oh, hi. Er... I want to find out about joining the club.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,800
Jim: Right. I can help you there. I'm the club secretary and my name's Jim Hunter.

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,700
Woman: Oh, hi Jim.

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:24,000
Jim: So, are you interested in membership for yourself?

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,900
Woman: That's right.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:31,452
Jim: OK. Well there are basically two types of adult membership.

8
00:00:31,452 --> 00:00:36,500
If you're pretty serious about cycling, there's the Full membership.

9
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,821
That costs 260 dollars and that covers you not just for ordinary cycling

10
00:00:42,821 --> 00:00:50,600
but also for races both here in the city and also in other parts of Australia.

11
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,007
Woman: Right. Well, I'm not really up to that standard.

12
00:00:54,007 --> 00:00:59,800
I was more interested in just joining a group to do some cycling in my free time.

13
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,780
Jim: Sure. That's why most people join

14
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:09,265
So, in that case you'd be better with the Recreational membership.

15
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:16,100
That's 108 dollars if you're over 19, and 95 dollars if you're under.

16
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,300
Woman: I'm 25.

17
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:24,340
Jim: OK. It's paid quarterly, and you can upgrade it later to the Full membership

18
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:26,500
if you want to, of course.

19
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,726
Now both types of membership include the club fee of 20 dollars.

20
00:01:31,726 --> 00:01:36,180
They also provide insurance in case you have an accident

21
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:40,000
though we hope you won't need that, of course.

22
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,608
Woman: No. OK, well, I'll go with the Recreational membership, I think.

23
00:01:44,608 --> 00:01:49,600
And that allows me to join in the club activities, and so on?

24
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:53,788
Jim: That's right. And once you're a member of the club,

25
00:01:53,788 --> 00:01:59,500
you're also permitted to wear our kit when you're out cycling. It's green and white.

26
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:05,200
Woman: Yes, I've seen cyclists wearing it. So, can I buy that at the club?

27
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:09,080
Jim: No, it's made to order by a company in Brisbane

28
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:15,406
You can find them online: they're called Jerriz.

29
00:02:15,406 --> 00:02:24,000
That's J-E-R-R-I-Z. You can use your membership number to put in an order on their website.

30
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,100
Woman: OK. Now, can you tell me a bit about the rides I can do?

31
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:33,888
Jim: Sure. So we have training rides pretty well every morning,

32
00:02:33,888 --> 00:02:43,900
and they're a really good way of improving your cycling skills as well as your general level of fitness, but they're different levels.

33
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:50,889
Level A is pretty fast - you're looking at about 30 or 35 kilometres an hour.

34
00:02:50,889 --> 00:02:55,082
If you can do about 25 kilometres an hour,

35
00:02:55,082 --> 00:03:00,584
you'd probably be level B, and then level C are the novices,

36
00:03:00,725 --> 00:03:04,400
who stay at about 15 kilometres per hour

37
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,900
Woman: Right. Well I reckon I'd be level B

38
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:11,300
So, when are the sessions for that level?

39
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,980
Jim: There are a couple each week

40
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:18,079
They're both early morning sessions. There's one on Tuesdays,

41
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:22,860
and for that one you meet at 5.30 am,

42
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:27,400
and the meeting point's the stadium - do you know where that is

43
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:33,300
Woman: Yes, it's quite near my home, in fact. OK, and how about the other one?

44
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:37,420
Jim: That's on Thursdays. It starts at the same time

45
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:40,900
but they meet at the main gate to the park.

46
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:44,300
Woman: Is that the one just past the shopping mall?

47
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,900
Jim: That's it.

48
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,700
Woman: So how long are the rides?

49
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:51,695
Jim: They're about an hour and a half.

50
00:03:51,695 --> 00:03:57,685
So, if you have a job it's easy to fit in before you go to work.

51
00:03:57,685 --> 00:04:00,100
And the members often go somewhere for coffee afterwards

52
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,300
so it's quite a social event.

53
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:07,180
Woman: OK. That sounds good. I've only just moved to the city

54
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:10,600
so I don't actually know many people yet.

55
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,800
Jim: Well, it's a great way to meet people.

56
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:16,900
Woman: And does each ride have a leader?

57
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:19,067
Jim: Sometimes, but not always.

58
00:04:19,067 --> 00:04:21,880
But you don't really need one

59
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:26,000
the group members on the ride support one another, anyway.

60
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,500
Woman: How would we know where to go?

61
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,400
Jim: If you check the club website

62
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:35,180
you'll see that the route for each ride is clearly marked.

63
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:40,004
So you can just print that out and take it along with you.

64
00:04:40,004 --> 00:04:45,200
It's similar from one week to another, but it's not always exactly the same.

65
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,500
Woman: And what do I need to bring?

66
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:51,318
Jim: Well, bring a bottle of water, and your phone.

67
00:04:51,318 --> 00:04:55,900
You shouldn't use it while you're cycling, but have it with you.

68
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,400
Woman: Right.

69
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:01,700
Jim: And in winter, it's well before sunrise when we set out

70
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:05,900
so you need to make sure your bike's got lights.

71
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:10,460
Woman: That's OK. Well, thanks Jim. I'd definitely like to join

72
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:13,900
So what's the best way of going about it?

73
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:16,000
Jim: You can...
